<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="52962" href="schedule/2017/spring/LLS/442/52962.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2017" href="schedule/2017.xml">2017</calendarYear><term id="120171" href="schedule/2017/spring.xml">Spring 2017</term><subject id="LLS" href="schedule/2017/spring/LLS.xml">Latina/Latino Studies</subject><course id="442" href="schedule/2017/spring/LLS/442.xml">Latina Literature</course></parents><sectionNumber>U  </sectionNumber><creditHours>3 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Topic:"Latina 'Pícaras' ('Outlaws')." A course on Latina women who throughout the ages have transgressed normalized and heteronormative boundaries from 17th century to contemporary times in film, narrative, and popular culture. From Lieutenant Nun: Memoire of Basque Transvestite in the New World  to The Hunger Games, we will read, watch and discuss some of the most daring accounts of women power in the Latinx tradition.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Undergrad - Urbana-Champaign.</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>B</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2017-03-13Z</startDate><endDate>2017-05-03Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>11:00 AM</start><end>01:20 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>133</roomNumber><buildingName>1207 W Oregon</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Quesada" firstName="S">Quesada, S</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>